  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The process of conversion of a concentrated ore into its oxide by heating in absence of or in limited supply of air is called calcination. It is usually done for hydroxide, hydrated oxides and carbonate&nbsp;ores.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MgCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></mover><mi>MgO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p>"
